Something strange happed in my current game... I'd just found a bones
level with a lot of stuff on it, and was trying to find out if some
rings were cursed or not.  So I dropped a few rings around and waited
to see if my dog stepped on them.  To make sure the pet stayed close to
me, I leashed it.  Anyway, the dog stepped on a ring, so I tried it on.
It was cursed!!!  Maybe being on the leash made the dog step on a cursed
object... anybody know?  Had to get a nymph steal the ring - all the
fountains dried up when I tried to #dip it.

This game is my best start with a wizard for a long time.  The main
reasons why I'm still alive are (i) ring of regeneration (started with
it) and (ii) the +4 cloak of displacement I found on level 1!  The
baddies sure have a tough time hitting me when I'm wearing the cloak.
Also have Fire Brand and Dragonbane from an altar - people have said
that Fire Brand / Frost Brand are better than Excalibur.  The problem
is that Fire Brand's fire damage won't do me much good in Hell, since
all monsters there are fire resistant... right?  Maybe I'll try to get
Frost Brand by sacrificing as well.

Another interesting item which I have is a flute - I assume it's a magic
flute, although I haven't id'd it yet.  When I #apply it and improvise,
I "produce soft music" and all monsters go to sleep.  I lost my first
pet this way - it wouldn't wake up!  After throwing food and objects at
it, even kicking it, I eventually just left it behind.  Questions: is the
sleep effect actually permanent?  I presume elves and such are immune.
Does the flute have only a certain number of charges, like a frost horn?
I thought a magic flute tamed monsters, rather than sending them to sleep,
or am I thinking of a magic harp?

